  "english": "CANON\nOF THE DORMITION [LITERALLY: TRANSLATION] OF THE HOLY MOTHER OF GOD\nON THE EVE, AND NIGHT\nThere is a vigil. They shall place the Holy Relics [or Sacrament] upon the cushion in the chancel.\nProcessional hymn, Tone 8 [d-k]: The East from the highest [Arevelk gerarpin].\nAnd the priests shall vest together and come into the chancel,\nAnd they shall begin: Canticle [of the Dawn], Tone 5 [g-3]: Today gathered [Aysor zhoghovyal] of the saints.\nAlleluia of the Nativity.\nPatristic Hymn [Harts], Tone 7 [d-dz]: Who [concerning] the first mother [Vor znaghamorn].\nMorning Song: Arise, O Lord, into Thy rest [Ari ter i hangist ko].\nLitanist: Holy Mother [Mayr surb].\nHoly God, Who came to the translation of Your mother and virgin.\nAnd they shall go outside with the Cross and Gospel and all ornaments in procession, singing the hymn:\nTone 5 [g-3] [originally written g-d-y-dz / g-3]: Today gathered [Aysor zhoghovyal].\nAfterward: Psalm 131 [132]: Arise, O Lord, into Thy rest. Antiphon: Remember, O Lord, David.\nScripture: Song of Songs 4:9: You have ravished my heart... to verse 15: from Lebanon; 8:14 [with additions]: The Lord made you... to verse 8:14: unblemished. This is a compilation.\nProphet Isaiah 7:10: And the Lord spoke again... to verse 16: he shall choose the good.\nEpistle: Galatians 3:29: And if you... to 4:7: heir of God.\nAlleluia: The Holy Spirit shall come.\nGospel: Luke 1:26: And in the [sixth] month... to verse 38: the angel departed from her.\nLitany: For the peace from above [Vasni verust].\nAnd they shall sign the four corners of the world [Andastan].\nAfterward: By Your Holy Cross [Surb khachivs]. Prayer: Guard us [Pahpanea].\nAnd then, hymn Tone 8 [d-k]: Only-begotten Jesus [Yisus miadzin].\nOf the Mother of God, of the Cross, Glory.\nPsalm 129 [130]: Let Thine ears be attentive. Antiphon: Out of the depths.\nGospel: John 11:1: Now a certain man was sick... to verse 46: which Jesus had done.\nFor the souls of the departed [Hogvotsn hangutsyelots]. Prayer: Christ, Son of God [Kristos vordi astutso].\nAnd afterward: Newly-created [Norasteghdzyal].\nLitany: Let us ask [Khndrestsuk]. Save [Ketso].\nPrayer: To Your all-powerful and wondrous Coming.\n\nAt the Midday Liturgy\nIntroit: Mother of God, unwedded [Astvatsatsin anharsnatsyal]. Antiphon: My soul doth magnify [Metsatsustse].\nHymn, Tone 3 [b-3]: Unfading Flower [Antaram tsaghik].\nThe Psalm and Scripture readings are the same as the Morning service.\nAlleluia: Arise, O Lord, into Thy rest.\nGospel: Luke 2:1: And it came to pass in those days... to verse 7: room in the inn.\nSanctus: Multitude [Bazmutyun].\n\nBut after the Divine Liturgy, they shall begin to perform the Order of the Blessing of Grapes.\nHymn, Tone 4 [b-k]: Glory to Your Holy Cross, Alleluia.\nPsalm: There was signed. Of the fruit of the corn.\nGlory to Your Holy Cross. The life-giving Cross.\nAfterward: Scripture: Proverbs 3:9: Honor the Lord... to verse 10: shall even burst out.\nProphet Isaiah 65:8: Thus saith the Lord... to verse 10: who have sought Me.\nEpistle: Hebrews 6:16: Brethren, those who have fled for refuge... to 7:7: is blessed of the better.\nAlleluia: Psalm 66 [67]: God be merciful.\nGospel: John 15:1: I am the true vine... to verse 8: My disciples.\nLitany: Let us give thanks to the Beneficent [Gohatsaruk zbare-]",
